 free online collection of mathematics educational materials.","https://math.libretexts.org/","A large amount of materials and many typical practice problems.",[174],{"contributorId":175,"name":176,"avatarUrl":177},"gwynerva","Peter Radko","/file/contributors/gwynerva/avatar.png","group",[180,263,271],{"type":181,"link":182,"title":183,"description":184,"quickLinks":185,"stats":258},"topic","/article/foundations/equations/elementary/","Elementary Equations","\n    Learn how to solve and transform elementary equations step by step.\n    Simple and visual, with clear examples and without memorizing a bunch of obscure rules.\n    This is a key foundational skill in mathematics and the exact sciences.\n  ",[186,194,201,208,215,222,230,237,244,251],{"link":187,"schemaName":188,"title":189,"quick":190,"seo":191,"description":193},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#equality","accent_term","Equality",{},{"title":192},"What is equality?","Two expressions with an equals sign \"=\" between them. Equality can be true (2 = 2) or false (2 = 0).",{"link":195,"schemaName":196,"title":197,"quick":198,"seo":199,"description":200},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#equality-false-true","diagram","True and false equality",{},{},"If identical objects stand on the sides of the = sign, then the equality is true. If different -- false.",{"link":202,"schemaName":188,"title":203,"quick":204,"seo":205,"description":207},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#equation","Equation",{},{"title":206},"What is an equation?","An equality in which there is one or more unknowns or variables.",{"link":209,"schemaName":188,"title":210,"quick":211,"seo":212,"description":214},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#equation-solution","Solving an Equation",{},{"title":213},"What does it mean to solve an equation?","\"Solutions\" or \"roots\" of an equation are numbers that, when substituted for unknowns, turn it into a true equality.\n          \"To solve an equation\" means to find all its roots and prove that there are no other roots.",{"link":216,"schemaName":217,"title":218,"quick":219,"seo":220,"description":221},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#same-action-rule","accent_statement","Same Action Rule",{},{},"If the same action is performed on both sides of a true equality, the resulting equality will also be true.",{"link":223,"schemaName":224,"title":225,"quick":226,"seo":227,"description":229},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#common-mistakes","list","Mistakes when solving equations",{},{"title":228},"Common mistakes when solving equations","A list of common mistakes that beginners make when solving equations.",{"link":231,"schemaName":232,"title":233,"quick":234,"seo":235,"description":236},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#why-solve-equations-1","heading","Why Solve Equations?",{},{},"A set of examples requiring the ability to solve equations to work with.",{"link":238,"schemaName":232,"title":239,"quick":240,"seo":241,"description":243},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#triangle-of-formulas","Triangle of Formulas",{},{"title":242},"Magic triangle of formulas","A mnemonic technique for memorizing simple formulas.",{"link":245,"schemaName":232,"title":246,"quick":247,"seo":248,"description":250},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#equations-in-life","Equations in Life",{},{"title":249},"Where are equations used in life?","A selection of problems and situations from real life that can be solved if translated into equations.",{"link":252,"schemaName":253,"title":254,"quick":255,"seo":256,"description":257},"/practice/foundations/equations/elementary/#linear-root","problems","Linear equations formula",{},{},"Formula by which you can very quickly find the root of any equation of the form Ax + B = 0.",{"elements":259},{"accent_term":260,"accent_statement":261,"accent_important":150,"problem":262},3,1,36,{"type":178,"link":264,"title":265,"description":266,"stats":267},"/group/foundations/e